  "id": "regulatory-focus-theory",
  "term": "regulatory focus theory",
  "definition": "Regulatory focus theory is a perspective used to explain how people proactively change their work through two motivational orientations: a promotion focus aimed at achieving gains and growth, and a prevention focus aimed at avoiding negative outcomes. In this view, behavior can be directed either toward adding and expanding job aspects or toward making changes that reduce risks and problems.",
